    "summary": "Stellar Truckin' jam, soaring PITB, and tight second‑set flow",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a high‑energy set with highlights like the Truckin' > Nobody’s Fault But Mine jam, a soaring 16‑minute Playing In The Band and inspired renditions of Stella Blue and He’s Gone. The second set flows smoothly through Mississippi Half‑Step, Loose Lucy and an expansive The Other One sequence. Soundboard recordings capture crisp instrument balance throughout.",
    "review": "On March 19, 1973 at Nassau Coliseum the Dead were firing on all cylinders. The first set builds momentum with a bright opening of The Promised Land and classic Americana numbers before launching into a blistering Playing In The Band that stretches past the 16‑minute mark, showcasing Jerry’s soaring leads and Phil’s thunderous bass work. A standout moment arrives in the second set when Truckin' segues into an inspired Nobody's Fault But Mine jam – a loose, exploratory stretch that feels both joyous and daring. From the plaintive beauty of Stella Blue to the raucous energy of Loose Lucy and the marathon The Other One > Eyes Of The World sequence, the band rides a seamless groove, anchored by Keith’s tasteful keyboards and Bill’s steady pulse. The encore caps it off with the familiar sing‑along fare of Casey Jones and One More Saturday Night, leaving the audience buzzing. Across all available soundboard tapes the mix is crisp and balanced, capturing every nuance of this high‑energy early‑’73 performance.",
